      ⍝ Regression
      ⍝
      1 > 0J0
1

      ⍝ regression (Bugs28 #81): two IntCells used to compare exactly
      ⍝ (==), while the very same two numbers stored as FloatCells
      ⍝ compared tolerantly via ⎕CT -- so 1000000000000000 =
      ⍝ 1000000000000001 (both integers) gave 0, but 1E15 =
      ⍝ 1000000000000001 (float vs. integer, same values) gave 1. ISO
      ⍝ 13751 tolerant equality (p. 19) has no integer exception.
      ⍝ IntCell::equal() now falls back to the same tolerant comparison
      ⍝ (after an exact-match fast path) instead of a bare ==. ⍳ (which
      ⍝ also uses Cell::equal()) is fixed the same way.
      ⍝
      1000000000000000=1000000000000001
1

      1E15=1000000000000001
1

      1000000000000000⍳1000000000000001
1

      1000000000000000=1000000000000000
1

      2=3
0

      ⍝ ==================================

